{
 "slug": "preparar/limpeza-e-tratamento",
 "modulo": "preparar",
 "tipo": "nb",
 "titulo": "4. Limpeza e tratamento",
 "nav": "4. Limpeza e tratamento",
 "sobretitulo": "Notebook mestre",
 "descricao": "Como deixar os dados prontos para análise e combinar tabelas?",
 "origem": {
  "material": "Notebook mestre",
  "trecho": "seção 4 (células 50 a 78)"
 },
 "html": "<blockquote class=\"destaque\">\n<p><strong>Regra de ouro:</strong> cada transformação deve ser <strong>intencional e documentada</strong>. Trabalhe sempre sobre <code>df</code>, com <code>df_original</code> guardado, e confirme o resultado após cada passo (<code>value_counts()</code>, <code>info()</code>, <code>shape</code>).</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-1\">4.1 Nomes de colunas e colunas irrelevantes</h2>\n<p><strong>O que faz:</strong> padroniza nomes (minúsculas, sem espaços) e remove colunas que não servem à análise.</p>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong> quando os nomes têm espaços, acentos ou maiúsculas misturadas, porque isso dificulta escrever <code>df['...']</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">df.columns = (df.columns</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">              .str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">strip</span>()</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\">              .str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">lower</span>()</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\">              .str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">replace</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\"> </span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">_</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\">              .str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">replace</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">-</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">_</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>))</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Renomear colunas específicas</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"8\">df = df.<span class=\"tk-fn\">rename</span>(columns={<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">nome_antigo</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>: <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">nome_novo</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>})          <span class=\"tk-com\"># nomes inexistentes são ignorados</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"9\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"10\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Remover colunas sem utilidade (ex.: 100% nulas, constantes, fora do escopo)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"11\">df = df.<span class=\"tk-fn\">drop</span>(columns=[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_irrelevante</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>], errors=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">ignore</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-2\">4.2 Conversão de tipos</h2>\n<p><strong>O que faz:</strong> corrige colunas lidas com o tipo errado. Os casos mais comuns são números como texto, datas como texto e categorias como texto livre.</p>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong> sempre que <code>df.info()</code> mostrar um tipo incoerente com o conteúdo.</p>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Texto -&gt; número, no formato brasileiro \"1.234,56\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_valor</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = pd.<span class=\"tk-fn\">to_numeric</span>(</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\">    df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_valor_texto</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\">      .str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">replace</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, regex=<span class=\"tk-kw\">False</span>)    <span class=\"tk-com\"># 1) remove o separador de milhar</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\">      .str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">replace</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">,</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, regex=<span class=\"tk-kw\">False</span>),  <span class=\"tk-com\"># 2) troca a vírgula decimal por ponto</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\">    errors=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coerce</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>,                        <span class=\"tk-com\"># valores inválidos viram NaN em vez de gerar erro</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\">)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"8\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"9\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Texto -&gt; data (informe o formato para evitar ambiguidade dia/mês)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"10\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_data</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = pd.<span class=\"tk-fn\">to_datetime</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_data</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>], <span class=\"tk-bi\">format</span>=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">%d</span><span class=\"tk-str\">/</span><span class=\"tk-str\">%</span><span class=\"tk-str\">m/</span><span class=\"tk-str\">%</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Y</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"11\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_data_fim</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = pd.<span class=\"tk-fn\">to_datetime</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_data_fim</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>], <span class=\"tk-bi\">format</span>=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">%d</span><span class=\"tk-str\">/</span><span class=\"tk-str\">%</span><span class=\"tk-str\">m/</span><span class=\"tk-str\">%</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Y</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"12\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"13\">df[[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_valor_texto</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_valor</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_data</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_data_fim</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]].dtypes</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">coluna_valor_texto               str\ncoluna_valor                 float64\ncoluna_data           datetime64[us]\ncoluna_data_fim       datetime64[us]\ndtype: object</pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--atencao\"><p class=\"callout__titulo\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icone\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span>O que observar</span></p><div class=\"callout__corpo\"><ul>\n<li>Só <code>.str.replace(',', '.')</code> funciona com <code>\"1234,56\"</code>, mas <strong>quebra</strong> com <code>\"1.234,56\"</code>. Remova o separador de milhar primeiro, ou resolva na leitura com <code>decimal=','</code> e <code>thousands='.'</code>.</li>\n<li>Com <code>errors='coerce'</code>, compare a quantidade de nulos antes e depois. Novos nulos indicam valores que não puderam ser convertidos e precisam ser investigados.</li>\n<li>Outros formatos de data: <code>'%Y-%m-%d'</code> (ISO), <code>'%d/%m/%Y %H:%M'</code>. Quando o formato varia, use <code>dayfirst=True</code>.</li>\n<li><code>df['coluna'].astype('string')</code> força o tipo texto (útil para garantir que todos os valores sejam strings). <code>astype('category')</code> economiza memória em colunas repetitivas.</li>\n</ul></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-3\">4.3 Tratamento de valores nulos</h2>\n<p><strong>O que faz:</strong> decide o destino dos nulos encontrados na Seção <a href=\"/preparar/primeira-inspecao/#secao-3-3\">3.3</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong> depois de entender <strong>por que</strong> os valores faltam. Escolha a estratégia conforme o caso:</p>\n<div aria-label=\"por que\" class=\"tabela\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Estratégia</th>\n<th>Código</th>\n<th>Quando usar</th>\n<th>Risco</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Remover linhas</td>\n<td><code>df.dropna(subset=['coluna'])</code></td>\n<td>poucos nulos (&lt; ~5%) e aleatórios</td>\n<td>perda de dados e viés, se o nulo não for aleatório</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Remover coluna</td>\n<td><code>df.drop(columns=...)</code></td>\n<td>coluna quase toda vazia</td>\n<td>perder variável útil</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Preencher categoria</td>\n<td><code>fillna('Não informado')</code></td>\n<td>categóricas: o \"não informado\" vira uma categoria visível</td>\n<td>nenhum, se for analisado como grupo próprio</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Preencher com mediana/moda</td>\n<td><code>fillna(df['col'].median())</code></td>\n<td>numéricas, quando um modelo exige dados completos</td>\n<td>reduz a variabilidade e cria picos artificiais</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sinalizar</td>\n<td><code>df['col'].isna().astype(int)</code></td>\n<td>quando o fato de faltar pode ser informativo</td>\n<td>nenhum, porque preserva a informação</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ignorar</td>\n<td>(não fazer nada)</td>\n<td>pandas e seaborn já ignoram NaN em cálculos e gráficos</td>\n<td>lembrar de reportar o <code>n</code> efetivo</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Categórica: nulo vira categoria explícita</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">fillna</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Não informado</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Numérica: sinaliza a ausência e mantém o NaN (os cálculos ignoram NaN)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num_ausente</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">isna</span>().<span class=\"tk-fn\">astype</span>(<span class=\"tk-bi\">int</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Remover linhas sem valor em colunas essenciais (exemplo; descomente se fizer sentido)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"8\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># df = df.dropna(subset=['coluna_num'])</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"9\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"10\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">value_counts</span>(dropna=<span class=\"tk-kw\">False</span>)   <span class=\"tk-com\"># confirma o resultado</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">coluna_cat\nA                494\nB                292\nC                189\nNão informado     30\nName: count, dtype: int64</pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-4\">4.4 Remoção de duplicados <span class=\"selo selo--complemento\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\" title=\"Técnica que não estava no material de estudo original\">Complemento</span></h2>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">n_antes = <span class=\"tk-bi\">len</span>(df)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">df = df.<span class=\"tk-fn\">drop_duplicates</span>()                                  <span class=\"tk-com\"># linha inteira igual</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># df = df.drop_duplicates(subset=['coluna_id'], keep='first')  # mesma chave</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Removidas </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>n_antes - <span class=\"tk-bi\">len</span>(df)<span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\"> linhas duplicadas</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">Removidas 5 linhas duplicadas</pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-5\">4.5 Recodificação de categorias</h2>\n<p><strong>O que faz:</strong> renomeia, agrupa e <strong>ordena</strong> categorias.</p>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>rótulos longos, inconsistentes ou pouco informativos (<code>'Prefer not to say'</code>, <code>'-'</code>);</li>\n<li>categorias ordinais que precisam aparecer na ordem lógica, e não alfabética, em tabelas e gráficos;</li>\n<li>muitas categorias raras que poluem a análise.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># 1) Mapear valores (map com dicionário: valores ausentes no dicionário viram NaN)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">mapa = {<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">baixo</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>: <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Baixo</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">médio</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>: <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Médio</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">alto</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>: <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Alto</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>}</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_ordinal</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_ordinal</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">map</span>(mapa)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># 2) Definir a ORDEM das categorias ordinais</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\">ordem = [<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Baixo</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Médio</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Alto</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_ordinal</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = pd.<span class=\"tk-fn\">Categorical</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_ordinal</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>], categories=ordem, ordered=<span class=\"tk-kw\">True</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"8\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"9\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_ordinal</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">value_counts</span>().<span class=\"tk-fn\">sort_index</span>()   <span class=\"tk-com\"># sort_index respeita a ordem definida</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">coluna_ordinal\nBaixo    289\nMédio    480\nAlto     231\nName: count, dtype: int64</pre></div>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># 3) Manter apenas categorias relevantes (ex.: com mais de 1% dos registros)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">freq = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">value_counts</span>(normalize=<span class=\"tk-kw\">True</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\">categorias_relevantes = freq[freq &gt; <span class=\"tk-num\">0.01</span>].index</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\">df_relevantes = df[df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">isin</span>(categorias_relevantes)]</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># 4) ... ou agrupar as categorias raras em 'Outros'</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat_agrupada</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">where</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">isin</span>(categorias_relevantes), <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Outros</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span></code></pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--atencao\"><p class=\"callout__titulo\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icone\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span>O que observar</span></p><div class=\"callout__corpo\"><ul>\n<li><code>map</code> transforma em <code>NaN</code> tudo o que não estiver no dicionário. Para trocar apenas alguns valores e manter o resto, use <code>replace</code>. Confira sempre com <code>value_counts(dropna=False)</code>.</li>\n<li>Antes de descartar categorias pouco informativas (<code>'Não informado'</code>, <code>'Prefer not to say'</code>), meça quanto elas representam. Se forem poucas (&lt; ~5%), ignorá-las raramente muda as conclusões.</li>\n<li>Uma alternativa improvisada para ordenar categorias é criar rótulos que já se ordenam alfabeticamente (<code>'[18 - 24]'</code>, <code>'[25 - 34]'</code>). <code>pd.Categorical(ordered=True)</code> é mais robusto.</li>\n</ul></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-6\">4.6 Colunas de texto e colunas multivaloradas</h2>\n<p><strong>O que faz:</strong> limpa texto e extrai informação de colunas com vários valores na mesma célula (ex.: <code>\"item_1;item_3\"</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong> quando <code>nunique()</code> é muito alto porque cada linha tem uma <strong>combinação</strong> de respostas.</p>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Limpeza básica de texto</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat_2</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat_2</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">strip</span>().str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">upper</span>()</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Flag: a linha contém um valor específico? (na=False trata nulos como \"não contém\")</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">contem_item_1</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_multivalor</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">contains</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">item_1</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, na=<span class=\"tk-kw\">False</span>).<span class=\"tk-fn\">astype</span>(<span class=\"tk-bi\">int</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Contagem de cada valor individual: split + explode (uma linha por valor)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"8\">contagem_itens = (df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_multivalor</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"9\">                  .str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">split</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">;</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"10\">                  .<span class=\"tk-fn\">explode</span>()</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"11\">                  .<span class=\"tk-fn\">value_counts</span>())</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"12\">contagem_itens</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">coluna_multivalor\nitem_4    508\nitem_1    507\nitem_3    506\nitem_2    484\nName: count, dtype: int64</pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--atencao\"><p class=\"callout__titulo callout__titulo--so-icone\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icone\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span class=\"sr-only\">Atenção</span></p><div class=\"callout__corpo\"><p><code>str.contains('item_1')</code> também encontra <code>'item_10'</code>. Para correspondência exata, use <code>explode</code> ou uma regex com limites, como <code>r'(^|;)item_1(;|$)'</code>. Outros métodos úteis: <code>str.startswith</code>, <code>str.endswith</code>, <code>str.lower</code>, <code>str.len</code>, <code>str.extract</code>.</p></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-7\">4.7 Filtros</h2>\n<p><strong>O que faz:</strong> seleciona linhas por condição.</p>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong> para recortar o escopo (período, segmento), excluir valores inválidos ou isolar casos para inspeção.</p>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">filtro_valor = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num_2</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] &gt; <span class=\"tk-num\">100</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">filtro_cat = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">isin</span>([<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">A</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">B</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>])</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\">filtro_texto = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].str.<span class=\"tk-fn\">startswith</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">A</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\">df_filtrado = df.loc[filtro_valor &amp; filtro_cat].<span class=\"tk-fn\">copy</span>()   <span class=\"tk-com\"># &amp; = E, | = OU, ~ = NÃO (use parênteses)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Equivalentes úteis</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"8\">df.loc[df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">between</span>(<span class=\"tk-num\">10</span>, <span class=\"tk-num\">20</span>)]                 <span class=\"tk-com\"># intervalo inclusivo</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"9\">df.<span class=\"tk-fn\">query</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num_2 &gt; 100 and coluna_cat == </span><span class=\"tk-str\">\"</span><span class=\"tk-str\">A</span><span class=\"tk-str\">\"</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)      <span class=\"tk-com\"># sintaxe de texto</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"10\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"11\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span><span class=\"tk-bi\">len</span>(df_filtrado)<span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\"> de </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span><span class=\"tk-bi\">len</span>(df)<span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\"> linhas (</span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span><span class=\"tk-bi\">len</span>(df_filtrado) / <span class=\"tk-bi\">len</span>(df)<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.1%</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">)</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">211 de 1000 linhas (21.1%)</pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--atencao\"><p class=\"callout__titulo\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icone\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span>O que observar</span></p><div class=\"callout__corpo\"><ul>\n<li>Dar nomes às condições (<code>filtro_valor</code>, <code>filtro_cat</code>) deixa a lógica legível e permite combiná-las.</li>\n<li>Use <code>.copy()</code> ao criar um DataFrame filtrado que será modificado depois. Isso evita o <code>SettingWithCopyWarning</code> e efeitos colaterais.</li>\n<li>Sempre reporte <strong>quantas linhas</strong> o filtro removeu.</li>\n</ul></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-8\">4.8 Criação de colunas</h2>\n<p><strong>O que faz:</strong> deriva novas variáveis (totais, indicadores, faixas) das existentes.</p>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong> quando a pergunta de negócio depende de uma medida que não existe pronta.</p>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Soma de colunas</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_total</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_valor</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] + df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num_2</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]                 <span class=\"tk-com\"># NaN em qualquer parcela -&gt; NaN</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># df['coluna_total'] = df[['coluna_valor', 'coluna_num_2']].sum(axis=1)     # trata NaN como 0</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Indicador binário a partir de uma condição</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">flag_cat_a</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = (df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] == <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">A</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>).<span class=\"tk-fn\">astype</span>(<span class=\"tk-bi\">int</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"8\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Condição com dois resultados</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"9\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">nivel</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = np.<span class=\"tk-fn\">where</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num_2</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] &gt; df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num_2</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">median</span>(), <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">acima_mediana</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">abaixo_mediana</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"10\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"11\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Faixas (discretização) de uma variável numérica</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"12\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">faixa_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = pd.<span class=\"tk-fn\">cut</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>], bins=[<span class=\"tk-num\">0</span>, <span class=\"tk-num\">5</span>, <span class=\"tk-num\">10</span>, <span class=\"tk-num\">20</span>, np.inf],</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"13\">                         labels=[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">0-5</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">5-10</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">10-20</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">20+</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>])</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"14\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># pd.qcut(df['coluna_num'], q=4) -&gt; faixas com a mesma quantidade de registros (quartis)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"15\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"16\">df[[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_valor</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num_2</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_total</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">flag_cat_a</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">nivel</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">faixa_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]].<span class=\"tk-fn\">head</span>()</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><div aria-label=\"Saída em tabela\" class=\"tabela\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\"><table class=\"tabela-dados\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\"></th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_valor</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_num_2</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_total</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">flag_cat_a</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">nivel</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">faixa_num</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">0</th>\n<td class=\"num\">1,995.77</td>\n<td class=\"num\">73.07</td>\n<td class=\"num\">2,068.84</td>\n<td class=\"num\">0</td>\n<td>abaixo_mediana</td>\n<td>5-10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">1</th>\n<td class=\"num\">1,236.47</td>\n<td class=\"num\">95.14</td>\n<td class=\"num\">1,331.61</td>\n<td class=\"num\">1</td>\n<td>acima_mediana</td>\n<td>10-20</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">2</th>\n<td class=\"num\">4,994.47</td>\n<td class=\"num\">111.55</td>\n<td class=\"num\">5,106.02</td>\n<td class=\"num\">0</td>\n<td>acima_mediana</td>\n<td>10-20</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">3</th>\n<td class=\"num\">1,155.97</td>\n<td class=\"num\">78.46</td>\n<td class=\"num\">1,234.43</td>\n<td class=\"num\">0</td>\n<td>abaixo_mediana</td>\n<td>5-10</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">4</th>\n<td class=\"num\">4,154.87</td>\n<td class=\"num\">438.00</td>\n<td class=\"num\">4,592.87</td>\n<td class=\"num\">1</td>\n<td>acima_mediana</td>\n<td>5-10</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-9\">4.9 Transformação logarítmica</h2>\n<p><strong>O que faz:</strong> comprime valores altos e reduz a assimetria à direita.</p>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>variáveis com <strong>cauda longa à direita</strong> (renda, preços, tempos, contagens grandes);</li>\n<li>quando um teste ou modelo pressupõe normalidade;</li>\n<li>quando poucos valores muito altos dominam o gráfico.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># log(0) é indefinido: filtre os valores &gt; 0 ou use log1p = log(1 + x)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">log_coluna_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] = np.<span class=\"tk-fn\">log</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">where</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] &gt; <span class=\"tk-num\">0</span>))</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># df['log_coluna_num'] = np.log1p(df['coluna_num'])   # alternativa quando há zeros</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\">df[[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">log_coluna_num</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]].<span class=\"tk-fn\">skew</span>()   <span class=\"tk-com\"># assimetria antes x depois (ver Seção 5.4)</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">coluna_num        1.89\nlog_coluna_num   -0.12\ndtype: float64</pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--atencao\"><p class=\"callout__titulo\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icone\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span>O que observar</span></p><div class=\"callout__corpo\"><ul>\n<li>Resultados na escala log são interpretados em termos <strong>relativos</strong>: uma diferença de 0,1 no log equivale a cerca de 10% de diferença no valor original.</li>\n<li>Para apresentar ao público, volte à escala original com <code>np.exp()</code>, ou use eixo logarítmico no gráfico: <code>ax.set_xscale('log')</code>.</li>\n</ul></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"secao-4-10\">4.10 Junção de tabelas <span class=\"selo selo--complemento\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\" title=\"Técnica que não estava no material de estudo original\">Complemento</span></h2>\n<p><strong>O que faz:</strong> combina duas tabelas por uma chave em comum (<code>merge</code>), por exemplo para trazer atributos de uma tabela de dimensão para a tabela principal.</p>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong> quando a informação necessária está espalhada em mais de uma tabela ou arquivo.</p>\n<div aria-label=\"Quando usar:\" class=\"tabela\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Tipo (<code>how=</code>)</th>\n<th>Mantém</th>\n<th>Uso típico</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>'left'</code></td>\n<td>todas as linhas da esquerda; sem correspondência → NaN</td>\n<td>enriquecer a tabela principal sem perder registros</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>'inner'</code></td>\n<td>só as chaves presentes nas duas</td>\n<td>analisar apenas o que existe nos dois lados</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>'outer'</code></td>\n<td>todas as chaves dos dois lados</td>\n<td>auditar diferenças entre tabelas</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>'right'</code></td>\n<td>todas as linhas da direita</td>\n<td>o mesmo que <code>left</code>, invertendo as tabelas</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">n_antes = <span class=\"tk-bi\">len</span>(df)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">df_com_categoria = df.<span class=\"tk-fn\">merge</span>(tabela_categorias, on=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, how=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">left</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>,</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\">                            validate=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">many_to_one</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)   <span class=\"tk-com\"># erro se a chave se repetir na tabela de dimensão</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Linhas antes: </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>n_antes<span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\"> | depois: </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span><span class=\"tk-bi\">len</span>(df_com_categoria)<span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Linhas sem correspondência:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, df_com_categoria[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_grupo</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">isna</span>().<span class=\"tk-fn\">sum</span>())</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\">df_com_categoria[[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_id</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_grupo</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_meta</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]].<span class=\"tk-fn\">head</span>()</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">Linhas antes: 1000 | depois: 1000\nLinhas sem correspondência: 30</pre><div aria-label=\"Saída em tabela\" class=\"tabela\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\"><table class=\"tabela-dados\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\"></th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_id</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_cat</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_grupo</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_meta</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">0</th>\n<td class=\"num\">1</td>\n<td>B</td>\n<td>grupo_1</td>\n<td class=\"num\">700,000.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">1</th>\n<td class=\"num\">2</td>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>grupo_1</td>\n<td class=\"num\">1,200,000.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">2</th>\n<td class=\"num\">3</td>\n<td>C</td>\n<td>grupo_2</td>\n<td class=\"num\">450,000.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">3</th>\n<td class=\"num\">4</td>\n<td>B</td>\n<td>grupo_1</td>\n<td class=\"num\">700,000.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">4</th>\n<td class=\"num\">5</td>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>grupo_1</td>\n<td class=\"num\">1,200,000.00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Diagnóstico: quais chaves existem só de um lado?</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">diagnostico = df[[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]].<span class=\"tk-fn\">drop_duplicates</span>().<span class=\"tk-fn\">merge</span>(</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\">    tabela_categorias[[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>]], on=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, how=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">outer</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>, indicator=<span class=\"tk-kw\">True</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\">diagnostico</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><div aria-label=\"Saída em tabela\" class=\"tabela\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\"><table class=\"tabela-dados\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\"></th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_cat</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">_merge</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">0</th>\n<td>A</td>\n<td>both</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">1</th>\n<td>B</td>\n<td>both</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">2</th>\n<td>C</td>\n<td>both</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">3</th>\n<td>D</td>\n<td>right_only</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">4</th>\n<td>Não informado</td>\n<td>left_only</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Consultar todos os registros de uma chave específica em outra tabela</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">valor_id = eventos[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_id_cliente</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].iloc[<span class=\"tk-num\">0</span>]</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\">eventos[eventos[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_id_cliente</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] == valor_id]</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><div aria-label=\"Saída em tabela\" class=\"tabela\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\"><table class=\"tabela-dados\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\"></th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_id_cliente</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_variante</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_data_evento</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_etapa</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">coluna_valor_pedido</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">0</th>\n<td class=\"num\">1</td>\n<td>controle</td>\n<td>2024-06-25</td>\n<td>etapa_1</td>\n<td class=\"num\">NaN</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th class=\"num\" scope=\"row\">1</th>\n<td class=\"num\">1</td>\n<td>controle</td>\n<td>2024-06-27</td>\n<td>etapa_2</td>\n<td class=\"num\">NaN</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--atencao\"><p class=\"callout__titulo\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icone\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span>O que observar</span></p><div class=\"callout__corpo\"><ul>\n<li>Confira <strong>sempre</strong> o número de linhas antes e depois. Um aumento em um <code>left</code> join significa chave duplicada na tabela da direita. <code>validate='many_to_one'</code> (ou <code>'one_to_one'</code>) transforma esse risco em erro explícito.</li>\n<li><code>indicator=True</code> cria a coluna <code>_merge</code> (<code>left_only</code>, <code>right_only</code>, <code>both</code>), ótima para auditar chaves sem correspondência.</li>\n<li>As chaves precisam ter o <strong>mesmo tipo e formato</strong> nas duas tabelas (<code>'001'</code> ≠ <code>1</code>, <code>'A '</code> ≠ <code>'A'</code>). Padronize antes de juntar (Seções <a href=\"#secao-4-2\">4.2</a> e <a href=\"#secao-4-6\">4.6</a>).</li>\n<li>Colunas com o mesmo nome nos dois lados recebem os sufixos <code>_x</code> e <code>_y</code>. Use <code>suffixes=('_principal', '_dimensao')</code> para nomes claros.</li>\n<li>Para empilhar tabelas com as mesmas colunas (por exemplo, um arquivo por mês), use <code>pd.concat([df_1, df_2], ignore_index=True)</code> (Seção <a href=\"/preparar/importacao-dos-dados/#secao-2-1\">2.1</a>).</li>\n</ul></div></aside>\n",
